GCMouse for Lullaby-Dormison, 2026-10-19, ported from WineForge 0.6.0.7 (commit 8051e02d, itself
Elvin Hayatov's WineHQ merge request !11799 at bfa3c0fdc2da; LGPL-2.1-or-later like Wine). The
GameController mouse code and its notice are kept as written; what differs: it is OFF unless the
Mac driver key UseGCMouse is Y or the environment variable LULLABY_GCMOUSE is 1, so that nothing
changes for a player before the A/B on a game.

winemac: read mouse movement through GCMouse as WM_INPUT.

With it on (macOS 14 or newer), relative movement comes from GameController on a high priority
queue and goes to Wine as MOUSE_MOVED_RAW, raw input without the main thread's event loop and
without AppKit's acceleration; the NSEvent path keeps cursor updates, buttons and the wheel, and is
not sent as movement a second time. With it off the engine behaves as Dormison ships it
(LinearMouse stays). No wineserver or ABI change; GameController is linked weakly.

